The attached image, Figure 5 from the Journal of Controlled Release article, illustrates how Nano-11 enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A, a dot plot, shows that when BMDCs are exposed to ovalbumin (OVA) complexed with Nano-11 (Nano-11+OVA), a much larger population of cells becomes positive for both Nano-11 and OVA compared to cells exposed to OVA or Nano-11 alone. Panel B, a histogram of FITC-OVA fluorescence, further confirms this by showing a significant rightward shift in the fluorescence intensity for BMDCs incubated with Nano-11+OVA, indicating a greatly increased amount of OVA per cell. This demonstrates Nano-11's ability to facilitate antigen delivery into dendritic cells.